@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
hide methods
hide empty members
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

title Library - conceptual model

class Address <<dataType>> {
  street
  city
  zip
  country
}

enum Genre {
  NOVEL
  POETRY
  SCIENCE
  CHILDREN
  ...
}

class Library {
  name
  address : Address
}

class Publisher {
  name
  address : Address
}

class Book {
  isbn {id}
  title
  publicationDate
  genre : Genre
}

class Author {
  firstName
  lastName
  email
}

class Ownership {
  copies {1..5}
}

Publisher "1" -- "0..*" Book : publishes >
Author "1..*" -- "0..*" Book : writes >
Author "0..*" -- "0..*" Publisher : has contract with >
Library "0..*" -- "0..*" Book : owns >
(Library, Book) .. Ownership

note right of Ownership
  <b>Ownership = one book title in one library</b>
  (attributes of the owns relationship, like "provides")

  • Book is the <b>type</b> (one ISBN), not a physical copy,
    so 5 copies are still <b>1</b> Ownership → not a multiplicity 1..5
  • <b>How many</b> is stored inside the class: copies {1..5}
  • Each library + book pair only once {unique}
end note

note bottom of Book
  When a new book is inserted:
  - its ISBN must not already exist in the system
  - every listed author must have a contract
    with the listed publisher
end note
@enduml